    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Factor each term",
        "body": "The $k$-th numerator term is $k\\cdot2k\\cdot4k=8k^3$ and the $k$-th denominator term is $k\\cdot3k\\cdot9k=27k^3$. So the fraction equals $\\dfrac{8(1^3+2^3+\\cdots+10^3)}{27(1^3+2^3+\\cdots+10^3)}=\\dfrac8{27}$.\n\n**Answer: (C) $\\frac8{27}$**"
