    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "$FBCE$ is a rectangle and $ABCD$ is a square of side 1 (with $A$ on $FB$ and $D$ on $EC$). The diagonal $FC$ meets $AD$ at $X$. If $AX$ has length $x$ then the value of $AF$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-1997-r1/q12.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$2(1-x)$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$\\frac{x}{1-x}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$\\frac1{4x^2}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\frac{2x^2}{1-x}$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$2x$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Similar triangles",
        "body": "Triangles $FAX$ and $FBC$ are similar ($AX\\parallel BC$). Hence $\\dfrac{AF}{FB}=\\dfrac{AX}{BC}=\\dfrac x1$. Since $FB=AF+AB=AF+1$, we get $AF=x(AF+1)$, so $AF(1-x)=x$ and $AF=\\dfrac{x}{1-x}$.\n\n**Answer: (B) $\\frac{x}{1-x}$**"
      }
    ],
