    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The figure shows the plan of a town where all the street blocks are square. In the middle of the town is a park with a diagonal road through it. Gloria walks every day from her house at $H$ to her school at $S$, always taking one of the shortest routes. The number of different shortest routes that she can choose is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-1997-r1/q15.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "10"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "18"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "24"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "E",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use the park diagonal",
        "body": "The diagonal road through the park is a shortcut: it is shorter than going around two sides of a block, and there are no other roads inside the park. So every shortest route uses the diagonal $PQ$. To reach $P$ from $H$ you go 2 blocks east and 2 blocks south: $\\binom42=6$ routes. From $Q$ to $S$ you go 3 blocks east and 1 block south: $\\binom41=4$ routes. Total $6\\times4=24$.\n\n**Answer: (E) 24**"
      }
    ],
