    "grade": "10-12",
    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "A circle touches the four sides of the square $ABCD$. $BEFG$ is a square of side 1 in the corner at $B$, with its vertex $F$ on the circle. The length of $AB$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-1997-r1/q16.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "$4+2\\sqrt2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "$2\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "$5\\sqrt2$"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "$\\frac52\\pi$"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "$4\\sqrt2+1$"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Use the diagonal through the centre",
        "body": "Let $R$ be the radius, so $AB=2R$ and the centre $O$ is at distance $\\sqrt2R$ from $B$. The diagonal $BO$ passes through $F$ (the far corner of the small square), and $BF=\\sqrt2$. Since $F$ is on the circle nearest to $B$, $OB=OF+FB$: $\\sqrt2R=R+\\sqrt2$. So $R=\\dfrac{\\sqrt2}{\\sqrt2-1}=\\sqrt2(\\sqrt2+1)=2+\\sqrt2$ and $AB=2R=4+2\\sqrt2$.\n\n**Answer: (A) $4+2\\sqrt2$**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
