    "grade": "10-12",
    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Noxolo walks from her home to Bizana and back home. Her brother George walks from Bizana to their home and back to Bizana. They both walk at constant speeds (not necessarily the same). They leave at exactly the same time and meet for the first time 7 km from Bizana. Each one continues on their way to their destination where they both turn around without any loss of time. They meet the second time 4 km from their home. The distance, in kilometers, from their home to Bizana is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "9"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "11"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "17"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "20"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "impossible to tell"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "C",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Compare distances walked",
        "body": "Let the distance from home to Bizana be $L$ km. Up to the first meeting the two together have covered $L$ km, and up to the second meeting (they meet again after each has reached the other end and turned back) together they have covered $3L$ km. Since each walks at a constant speed, each has walked exactly three times as far as at the first meeting. George walked 7 km up to the first meeting, so he has walked $21$ km at the second meeting. In those 21 km he walked from Bizana to their home ($L$ km) and then 4 km back towards Bizana: $L+4=21$, so $L=17$.\n\n**Answer: (C) 17 km**"
      },
      {
        "title": "Check with Noxolo",
        "body": "With $L=17$, Noxolo has walked $3(L-7)=30$ km at the second meeting. She went from home to Bizana (17 km) and then back $17-4=13$ km towards home: $17+13=30$. The two accounts agree.\n\n**Answer: (C)**"
      }
    ],
