    "points": 5,
    "timeMinutes": null,
    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The diagonals of the quadrilateral $ABCD$ intersect at the point $E$. The area of triangle $AEB$ is 6, that of triangle $DEC$ is 24, and the areas of triangles $AED$ and $BEC$ are equal. The area of triangle $AED$ is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/senior-1997-r1/q19.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "15"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "18"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "20"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "30"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "A",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Ratios of areas",
        "body": "Triangles sharing a vertex and with bases on the same line have areas in the ratio of their bases. So $\\dfrac{[AED]}{[AEB]}=\\dfrac{DE}{EB}$ and $\\dfrac{[DEC]}{[BEC]}=\\dfrac{DE}{EB}$. With $[AED]=[BEC]=x$: $\\dfrac x6=\\dfrac{24}x$, so $x^2=144$ and $x=12$.\n\n**Answer: (A) 12**"
      }
    ],
